  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Integrating participatory story gathering into agroecology &amp; climate resilience learning journey</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">As part of the CAFOD Agroecology learning journey we propose an integration of participatory storytelling in partnership with Re-Alliance. Storytelling in film and photography will provide meaningful qualitative context to the monitoring process, visually showing the land and community transformations throughout the lifetime of the programme and beyond. Further still, making this a participatory process will allow farmers to share stories that are meaningful and relevant for their communities, giving insights as to what indicators are most appropriate for
community-based agroecology programming. Re-Alliance will support with design of the initiative, as well as training and mentoring for partners.</narrative>
  </description>
